\section*{S1. Frozen prompts, parsing, and answer isolation}

The exact Qwen P0 template is:

\begin{quote}\small\ttfamily\raggedright
You analyze a piping and instrumentation diagram (P\&ID). Answer only from the
visible diagram. Return only the final answer, without explanation or
Markdown.\\[2pt]
Question: \{question\}
\end{quote}

The matched InternVL prompt uses the same sentence sequence; image conditions
prepend the model's \texttt{<image>} placeholder, while the no-image condition
does not. All generation is greedy. Qwen contrasts label maximum image side and
output cap separately. InternVL image conditions label realised 448-pixel tile
count and output cap. The Transformers Mistral-tokenizer warning is resolved by
setting \texttt{fix\_mistral\_regex=true}; the warned first pass is retained as
a diagnostic artifact but is not scored or reported as the extension result.

Strict value scoring lowercases, trims, de-duplicates, sorts, and compares tag
sets. The conservative semantic grammar accepts alphabetic prefixes followed
by numeric, hyphen-numeric, or space-numeric suffixes (for example
\texttt{KL-58999}, \texttt{UV-00-001}, \texttt{SDL 299}, and \texttt{CV1});
bare uppercase tags are accepted after a frozen stopword filter. Empty strings
and \texttt{[]} map to an empty set. The parser never reads the hidden truth.
The answer-isolation audit covers @@AUDIT_INPUTS@@ public manifests and
@@AUDIT_OUTPUTS@@ primary E2--E8 raw output files. Every successful output's
legacy \texttt{answer} field aliases generated \texttt{raw} text rather than a
reference label.

\section*{S2. Five split diagnostics}

The L5 diagnostic is an exact image-SHA-256 plus released-template semantic
cache with a training-only task-majority fallback. There is no learned
embedding, neighbour count, or use of \texttt{source\_id} as a cache key.
The separate training-only task-majority prior scores @@PRIOR@@ aggregate
strict accuracy on Set B. This high aggregate calibration value is retained
because it motivates task-level reporting; it is not compared to tag F1 as if
the two outcomes measured the same quantity.

