\section*{S6. Complete reference-free fusion rule family}

Fusion uses only the frozen predicted Qwen and geometry-joined OCR tag sets.
No reference, score, confidence threshold, or fitted parameter enters a fused
prediction. The four simple rules were fixed as a complete reporting family
for this descriptive post-hoc analysis; no rule is omitted because of its
direction.

\begin{table}[H]
\centering
\caption{All component and fusion operating points on the same 100 value
records. Exact is strict set accuracy.}
\small
\begin{tabular}{lrrrr}
\toprule
Mode & Precision & Recall & F1 & Exact \\
\midrule
Qwen correct image & @@QWEN_P@@ & @@QWEN_R@@ & @@QWEN_F1@@ & @@QWEN_EXACT@@ \\
PaddleOCR geometry join & @@OCR_P@@ & @@OCR_R@@ & @@OCR_F1@@ & @@OCR_EXACT@@ \\
Set union & @@UNION_P@@ & @@UNION_R@@ & @@UNION_F1@@ & @@UNION_EXACT@@ \\
Set intersection & @@INTERSECTION_P@@ & @@INTERSECTION_R@@ & @@INTERSECTION_F1@@ & @@INTERSECTION_EXACT@@ \\
OCR if non-empty, otherwise Qwen & @@OCR_FALLBACK_P@@ & @@OCR_FALLBACK_R@@ & @@OCR_FALLBACK_F1@@ & @@OCR_FALLBACK_EXACT@@ \\
Qwen if non-empty, otherwise OCR & @@QWEN_FALLBACK_P@@ & @@QWEN_FALLBACK_R@@ & @@QWEN_FALLBACK_F1@@ & @@QWEN_FALLBACK_EXACT@@ \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

Union minus Qwen F1 is @@UNION_QWEN_DIFF@@
(@@UNION_QWEN_DIFF_CI@@), and union minus OCR is @@UNION_OCR_DIFF@@
(@@UNION_OCR_DIFF_CI@@). Intersection exchanges recall for precision rather
than improving F1. OCR-first fallback minus OCR is @@OCR_FALLBACK_OCR_DIFF@@
(@@OCR_FALLBACK_OCR_DIFF_CI@@). These comparisons are descriptive and require
prospective validation on another drawing family.

